{"architectures":["arm64","x64","x86"],"id":"oxc-project.oxfmt","latestVersion":"0.69.0","media":{"icons":[],"screenshots":[]},"package":{"description":"Oxfmt is a high-performance formatter for the JavaScript ecosystem.","license":"MIT","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/oxc-project/oxc/blob/HEAD/LICENSE","locale":"en-US","localizations":{"en-US":{"description":"Oxfmt is a high-performance formatter for the JavaScript ecosystem.","license":"MIT","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/oxc-project/oxc/blob/HEAD/LICENSE","locale":"en-US","longDescription":"Oxfmt is a high-performance formatter for the JavaScript ecosystem.\n\n- Supported languages\nJavaScript, JSX, TypeScript, TSX, JSON, JSONC, JSON5, YAML, TOML, HTML, Angular, Vue, CSS, SCSS, Less, Markdown, MDX, GraphQL, Ember, Handlebars\n\n- Built for scale\nOxfmt targets large codebases and CI environments, with an emphasis on high throughput and predictable performance.\nIt is built on the Oxc compiler stack and avoids architectural bottlenecks common in existing formatter implementations.\nOur benchmarks show Oxfmt to be approximately 30x faster than Prettier and 2x faster than Biome.\n\n- Batteries included\n  - Oxfmt includes built-in features that typically require external Prettier plugins:\n  - Import sorting\n  - Tailwind CSS class sorting\n  - package.json field sorting\n  - Embedded formatting (CSS-in-JS, GraphQL, etc.)\n\n- Prettier-compatible\nOxfmt integrates into existing Prettier-based workflows.\nThe oxfmt CLI behaves similarly to Prettier by default, allowing adoption with minimal changes to scripts and tooling.\nOxfmt matches Prettier’s JavaScript formatting. When migrating from recent versions of Prettier, formatting differences should not occur; any differences are considered bugs.\nOxfmt currently passes approximately 95% of Prettier's JavaScript and TypeScript test suite. The remaining cases are niche scenarios, and we work with the Prettier team to converge on formatting over time.\nNo additional dependencies or configuration needed.","moniker":"oxfmt","name":"oxfmt","packageUrl":"https://oxc.rs/docs/guide/usage/formatter.html","publisher":"VoidZero Inc. & Contributors","publisherUrl":"https://voidzero.dev/","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/oxc-project/oxc/releases/tag/apps_v1.84.0","tags":["formatter","javascript","typescript"]}},"longDescription":"Oxfmt is a high-performance formatter for the JavaScript ecosystem.\n\n- Supported languages\nJavaScript, JSX, TypeScript, TSX, JSON, JSONC, JSON5, YAML, TOML, HTML, Angular, Vue, CSS, SCSS, Less, Markdown, MDX, GraphQL, Ember, Handlebars\n\n- Built for scale\nOxfmt targets large codebases and CI environments, with an emphasis on high throughput and predictable performance.\nIt is built on the Oxc compiler stack and avoids architectural bottlenecks common in existing formatter implementations.\nOur benchmarks show Oxfmt to be approximately 30x faster than Prettier and 2x faster than Biome.\n\n- Batteries included\n  - Oxfmt includes built-in features that typically require external Prettier plugins:\n  - Import sorting\n  - Tailwind CSS class sorting\n  - package.json field sorting\n  - Embedded formatting (CSS-in-JS, GraphQL, etc.)\n\n- Prettier-compatible\nOxfmt integrates into existing Prettier-based workflows.\nThe oxfmt CLI behaves similarly to Prettier by default, allowing adoption with minimal changes to scripts and tooling.\nOxfmt matches Prettier’s JavaScript formatting. When migrating from recent versions of Prettier, formatting differences should not occur; any differences are considered bugs.\nOxfmt currently passes approximately 95% of Prettier's JavaScript and TypeScript test suite. The remaining cases are niche scenarios, and we work with the Prettier team to converge on formatting over time.\nNo additional dependencies or configuration needed.","moniker":"oxfmt","name":"oxfmt","packageUrl":"https://oxc.rs/docs/guide/usage/formatter.html","publisher":"VoidZero Inc. & Contributors","publisherUrl":"https://voidzero.dev/","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/oxc-project/oxc/releases/tag/apps_v1.84.0","tags":["formatter","javascript","typescript"]},"schemaVersion":1,"source":"winget","versions":[{"architectures":["arm64","x64","x86"],"detailPath":"versions/0.69.0/app.json","detailSha256":"2f4a8e93a128b0df85cbee4d5647a2ced0cc88cebe52e2341d3a69be17789b5b","releaseDate":"2026-09-21","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"0.69.0"},{"architectures":["arm64","x64","x86"],"detailPath":"versions/0.68.0/app.json","detailSha256":"d3119c200d03f2d8bd960859a8f12b24a3fe6937b05fbf51b932ea76b9955850","releaseDate":"2026-09-14","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"0.68.0"},{"architectures":["arm64","x64","x86"],"detailPath":"versions/0.67.0/app.json","detailSha256":"aa668b0fd971162b365d866538e382cf8e1e31d596017b69af6a306c99f93365","releaseDate":"2026-09-07","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"0.67.0"},{"architectures":["arm64","x64","x86"],"detailPath":"versions/0.66.0/app.json","detailSha256":"42f69b23f393648bd0936e70930ce186acb474a67d7204235aba6b0b8ee95585","releaseDate":"2026-09-01","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"0.66.0"},{"architectures":["arm64","x64","x86"],"detailPath":"versions/0.65.0/app.json","detailSha256":"071da9f98c3760c2eb6037b0e8809c04ad40cba50cd96537cc505ab855210b94","releaseDate":"2026-08-24","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"0.65.0"},{"architectures":["arm64","x64","x86"],"detailPath":"versions/0.64.0/app.json","detailSha256":"13bf696783ee67d4719174648c987b433502ed4cf1cd5faa27b1528754ba2c41","releaseDate":"2026-08-18","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"0.64.0"},{"architectures":["arm64","x64","x86"],"detailPath":"versions/0.63.0/app.json","detailSha256":"e58ab5e7287e9132234e074f88ad130b96f67790c198c70271b5d7cd19d9d0a7","releaseDate":"2026-08-10","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"0.63.0"},{"architectures":["arm64","x64","x86"],"detailPath":"versions/0.62.0/app.json","detailSha256":"40a8c247192bc874588088020a62d